-- A string with no closing quote.
--
-- Bound rather than interpolated, and plan 64 leaf 6 is why it had to be:
-- the migration put this literal inside `#{…}`, where the *interpolation*
-- scanner reaches the end of the line first and `RDX0005` is what the author
-- sees. A fixture for `RDX0003` has to keep the bad literal where the string
-- scanner meets it — which `code_coverage` said, by reporting the code as
-- declared and unreached.
main : ()
